1. The parking system supports multiple types of vehicles (motorcycles, cars, trucks)
2. The parking system supports multiple types of parking spots (compact, regular, oversized)
3. The parking system needs to issue a parking ticket on vehicle entry & log the duration for which the vehicle was parked.
4. Customers need to pay a fee (parking-fee) during exit depending on vehicle size & duration & time-of-the-day.


Core objects

1. Vehicle (size, license-plate) represent a vehicle that needs a parking-spot.
2. ParkingSpot (size, id) represents the spot where vehicle is parked.
3. Ticket (Vehicle, ParkingSpot, id, start-time, end-time) represents the ticket issued to customer on entry.
4. ParkingManager
5. ParkingLot